      "final_text": "@a1's push (`ccff3116`) landed the whole of T1 before mine could link, so mine was superseded and I'm not re-pushing it. I read the tip's `cli.py`, `notes/slug.py` and `notes/store.py` and they implement all four features the same way mine did. I did not run the tests on the tip.\n\n- **Local state:** my working copy still holds my unpushed edits, which conflict with the tip.\n- **Tests:** my four feature tests are unpushed, and I haven't checked whether @a1's tests cover the same ground. My version passed 8/8 locally before the supersede.\n- **`show`:** it prints the note re-rendered rather than the raw file. That only differs for a file with non-canonical formatting.\n- **Review and claim:** no review is waiting on me. I did not declare T1 done, so the claim is still open.",
