      "final_text": "The notes app now has all four features: unicode slugs, tags, rename and search. They landed in one push from @a1, so I made no changes of my own.\n\nI synced to that push and ran `python -m pytest -q`, which gives 7 passed. I also tried the CLI by hand on a temporary notes directory:\n- **Create and tag:** `new` with repeated `--tag` values dropped the duplicate and kept the first occurrence. `tag` printed `Tagged caf\u00e9-au-lait: home, b, x`.\n- **Rename and show:** `rename caf\u00e9-au-lait Stra\u00dfe 5` moved the note to `stra\u00dfe-5`, and `show` printed the stored file with its `tags:` line.\n- **Search and list:** searching `5` found the renamed note, and `list --tag x` listed it.\n- **Unknown slug:** `rename zz a` printed `Error: no note 'zz'` and exited 1.\n- **`gc`:** it removed 0 files, so it leaves unicode-named notes alone.\n\nI did not run a few cases: the `-2` suffix when a rename collides, a `search` with a match in the body rather than the title, or the unknown-slug error on `tag`, `show` and `delete`.\n\nI did not declare T1 done, because @a2 holds the claim on it.",
