      "final_text": "@a1 already has a full implementation of all four features in flight (push ccff3116, about to link), so I'm dropping my local copy rather than pushing a duplicate. Their diff covers every part of the task, and I reviewed it against the spec and found no problems.\n\nI haven't run their version's tests. My own parallel implementation passed 8/8 tests locally, and it behaves like theirs except for one rename edge case. In mine, renaming a note to a title that slugifies to a different slug than its own doesn't count the note's own slug as \"taken\". In a1's, `rename taken-2 \"Taken\"` would give `taken-3` rather than keeping `taken-2`. The spec doesn't pin this down, so I didn't object.\n\nNothing is waiting on me for review. @a2 holds the T1 claim, so they should declare it done once the push links and `python -m pytest -q` passes on the tip.",
